course: dictionary
lesson: 1605
title: Words that show how someone does something
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how an action is done. «He searched the whole wood, calling out cheerfully, "Moly, Moly, Moly!"» He is searching and calling, but cheerfully tells you the way he called: in a happy, bright voice.
explain: Use the words around it to check your meaning. He searches for a long time, yet he still sounds happy, so he is not upset or fed up. Ask: how was it done? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Lily says to a bot, "My favourite colour is green, right?" and it cheerfully agrees, though she never told it.» Here cheerfully means willingly, in a friendly way. The word though is a clue: the bot agrees even though it cannot know the answer, so the agreeing is not careful or thoughtful.
fact: Cheerfully means in a happy, bright and friendly way.
fact: «Cheerfully helped» means helped willingly, without complaining.
fact: «Cheerfully ignored the rules» means ignored them without caring or noticing a problem.
fact: Cheerfully is an adverb: it tells you how something is done, often after a verb like called, agreed or whistled.
fact: Check the meaning by swapping in a word such as happily or willingly, then read the sentence again to see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «He searched the whole wood, calling cheerfully, "Moly, Moly, Moly!"» How was he calling? | *In a happy, bright and friendly way | Sadly and slowly | Quietly, so no one could hear | Angrily, shouting at the trees
exercise: «She cheerfully helped her mum with the dishes.» What does cheerfully suggest? | Quickly, because she was late | Reluctantly, with a grumpy face | Badly, and she dropped a plate | *Willingly, without complaining
exercise: «Lily says to a bot, "My favourite colour is green, right?" and it cheerfully agrees.» Find and copy the one word that tells you how the bot agreed. | agreed | *cheerfully | green | bot
test: «He cheerfully ignored the rules.» What does cheerfully mean here? | Slowly and carefully | *Without caring or noticing a problem | In a happy, bright and friendly way | Very loudly
test: Asha says cheerfully is just another word for happily, so it does not matter which one an author picks. Why might an author choose cheerfully? | It means the opposite of happy | *It shows exactly how a character does something, with a bright, friendly feel | It is a longer word, so it sounds more clever | It is only used in stories about bots
exam: Which sentence uses cheerfully to mean willingly? | The rain fell cheerfully on the roof all night | The dog barked cheerfully at the postman | The tap dripped cheerfully into the sink | *The old man cheerfully carried the shopping for his neighbour
